# [[.Label]]

A module for [Kosatka CMS](https://github.com/kosatka-cms/kosatka): a page
at `/[[.URLPath]]`.

## Develop

```bash
go mod tidy
go test ./...
```

| Path | What's there |
|---|---|
| `[[.Name]].go` | registers the module when the package is imported |
| `manifest.go` | its name, label and description on the Modules page |
| `wire.go`, `controller.go` | its route and page |
| `templates/`, `static/`, `translations/` | built into the binary |

Next steps - a table of its own, an install step, blocks, demo content:
[Write a module](https://kosatka-cms.github.io/kosatka/modules/write-a-module/),
[The module SDK](https://kosatka-cms.github.io/kosatka/modules/sdk/).

## Add it to a site

In the site's own main package (its binary calls `kosatka.Main`):

```bash
app module add [[.Path]]@v0.1.0
```

Before a release, try it from its directory: `replace [[.Path]] => ../<its directory>`
in the site's `go.mod`. Rebuild the binary and deploy it, then enable the
module on the Modules page.
